<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Summon Demon</h1>
<p>Sphere: Summoning Sphere
Class: Conjurer (guild level 40)
Mana: 30
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre><a cmd='#'>cast summon demon</a>
</pre>
<p>A large portal of fire opens, and a lesser demon (level 60) steps through to 
serve you, far stronger than any elemental. It follows you, fights beside you 
when you are in a fight, and when your hit points drop below a third it tries 
to rescue you. Like the elementals, it stays only a short time, from half a 
minute to a minute and a half, and doesn't take orders.
</p><p>Beware: if the spell fails, you lose control of the portal. The demon comes 
through unbound, thanks you for bringing it here, and attacks you. Even 
unbound, it goes back after a while, the longer the worse the spell 
failed, and banish can send it back sooner (see <a cmd='#'>Help Banish</a>).
</p><p>You must be standing. It is also found on scrolls.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Summon Devil</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Summon Fire</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Summoning Sphere</a>
</pre>




</div>